# 000-APP-0072 — Browsing for the background's picture in `wm`'s Settings — done

**Type:** tools · **Owner:** tools track (`APP`) · **Priority:** P2 · **Status:** done (2026-10-14) · **Blocked by:** — · **Main task:** — · **Roadmap:** track G · **Constitution:** MC-11.5

**Recorded by:** the tools track, 2026-10-14. The maintainer: "When selecting an image for the background we need a browse menu."

## Problem

The background's `Image file` row in Settings ([000-APP-0048](../issues/000-APP-0048-wm-settings.md), [000-APP-0050](../issues-done/000-APP-0050-wm-background-pictures-and-pattern-settings.done)) takes only a typed path. One has to know the file's name and directory, and a typo leaves the pattern with a notice.

## Plan

- `wm/src/settings.rs`: a browser over the file system. Enter on an empty `Image file` row, or F3 on it, opens it in the directory of the file named (else `data/`, else the boot disk's root).
  - It lists `..` below a root, then the directories, then the pictures (`.bmp`, `.png`, `.jpg`, `.jpeg`), each sorted. The boot disk's root also lists `ram:`.
  - ↑↓ PgUp PgDn Home End choose. Enter opens a directory, or takes a picture as the background, saved as any other change. Backspace goes up. Esc goes back to the rows.
  - A click on an entry does what Enter does on it; a click outside the window goes back. A click on the empty row opens the browser.
  - The line under the list says how many pictures are here, or why the directory cannot be read.
- `wm/src/main.rs`: the browser reads directories through `mind::fs::list`. `wm` holds the boot disk's files already (`REQUEST_FILES`), so no new authority is asked for.
- `wm`'s status line names the directory and the entry chosen (`BROWSE=<dir>:<name>`), for the tests.
- `docs/tools` (EN, RU).

## Acceptance criteria

- `tests/wm_host.rs`:
  - Enter on the empty row opens the browser in `data/`, with `..`, a directory and the pictures, without other files;
  - a directory opens, `..` comes back with the cursor on it, and `ram:` is listed at the root;
  - Enter on a picture sets the image and its file, and saves it;
  - Esc goes back; a click on an entry acts as Enter, outside the window goes back, on the empty row browses;
  - a directory that cannot be read says so.
- The `wm` suite: Enter on the empty `Image file` row opens the browser at `data/`; Esc goes back; F3 opens it again; Enter on `sky.jpg` sets `background = image data/sky.jpg`; the picture row puts the setting back.

## Related

[000-APP-0048](../issues/000-APP-0048-wm-settings.md) (Settings), [000-APP-0050](../issues-done/000-APP-0050-wm-background-pictures-and-pattern-settings.done) (pictures), [000-APP-0056](../issues-done/000-APP-0056-every-entry-of-wms-menu-reacts.done) (every row reacts).

## Resolution

- `wm/src/settings.rs`: `Browser` lists a directory's subdirectories and pictures (BMP, PNG, JPEG), from `data/`, and the boot disk's root lists `ram:`. Enter on the empty `Image file` row, F3 or a click opens it. Enter opens a directory or takes a picture, saved as any change. Backspace goes up and Esc goes back. A click on an entry acts as Enter.
- `wm/src/main.rs` reads directories through `mind::fs::list` with the files `wm` already holds; the state line names `BROWSE=<dir>:<entry>`.
- Tests: `tests/wm_host.rs` `the_picture_is_chosen_by_browsing`; the `wm` suite's `settings_react` browses `data/`, goes back, takes `sky.jpg` and puts the setting back.
- Commit 9d9c5e0; `docs/tools` (EN, RU).
- The gate of eda1c74 (2026-10-14): every local group (scripts/ci_local.sh, x86 and host); the x86 groups on PCU through Effector, with Secure Boot on i9 (PCU has no `python3-virt-firmware`) and the reproducible build on DESKTOP-i7-930-wsl-u24 (an hour was not enough on PCU); the aarch64 groups on DESKTOP-i7-930-wsl-u24, with "files, network and TLS" on un-rizen-service (the store's check outran its 240 s on the slower machine, [requests-STO.md](../issues/requests-STO.md)). All under TCG; tests, not proofs (MC-12.2).
